      "id": 1,
      "text": "Katsushika Ward was officially founded on March 15, 1947, in the heart of Tokyo's eastern edge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katsushika"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The ward is the setting for Japan's longest-running manga series, Kochira Katsushika-ku Kameari Kōen-mae Hashutsujo.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katsushika"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "At Yotsugi Station, a bronze statue of Captain Tsubasa celebrates the manga's creator and his hometown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://livejapan.com/en/in-tokyo/in-pref-tokyo/in-shibamata_kita-senju_kameari/article-a0005880/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Outside Shibamata Station stands a statue of Tora-san, the iconic character from the long-running film series.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katsushika"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Monchhichi Park occupies the former Sekiguchi toy factory site, echoing Katsushika's historic toy‑town legacy.",
